{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7d9ee08351c261685ebba2c661785002e0cd02f83d7866dc34edaa1545d5e8c0","digest":{"component_or_area":"docs/local-dev-env.md","key_entities":["docs/local-dev-env.md","tests/conftest.py","pytest_sessionfinish","_no_repo_root_leaks","_no_repo_commits","git status --porcelain","REPO ISOLATION FAILURE"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","test guard","repo isolation","concurrent writes","session-level backstop","local development"],"propositions":["The documentation for local development environment validation omits the session-level working-tree backstop guard from the list of concurrent-write misfire conditions.","The pytest_sessionfinish session-level backstop in tests/conftest.py diffs git status output across the entire session and fires at session end rather than per-test.","The session-level backstop reports as a REPO ISOLATION FAILURE at run tail instead of blaming an individual straddling test.","The documentation must list this third guard alongside the two per-test guards (_no_repo_root_leaks and _no_repo_commits) to give readers complete visibility of the guard family."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787899804467498001,"uuid":"8d64b482-43c6-4244-8466-94f3b8dd4a04"}